<title>UK: Guinness says LVMH claim lacks legal basis.</title>
<headline>Guinness says LVMH claim lacks legal basis.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>British drinks group Guinness Plc said on Friday proceedings taken against its planned merger with Grand Metropolitan Plc made by French drinks and luxury goods company LVMH Moet Hennessey Louis Vuitton SA lacks any legal basis.</p>
<p>&quot;Guinness is clear that LVMH's claim that the proposed merger of GrandMet and Guinness would constitute a 'control event' lacks any legal basis, and is confident that the ICC (International Chamber of Commerce) arbitration will find accordingly,&quot; said the company in a statement.</p>
</text>
